 instructions pi (Tc(pi)), where i = 1 n, and is calculated as shown in (9) Tc(pi) is obtained by calculating the number of clusters in the critical path of the custom instructions. For example; Tc of the custom instruction in Figure 4(a) is 2 Note that we have assumed that the delay of each cluster is equivalent to two software clock executions. This is a reasonable   assumption as the FPGA logic can generally   execute at significantly higher clock frequency than a commercially available soft processor core cycle"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"formula","orig":"ESCS Efficiency 8) ARFU ESCS = F(p;)x(Tsw (p;)-2-Tc(p;))","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":395.6666666666667,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":190.33333333333334,"r":362.3333333333333,"t":458.6666666666667},"charspan":[0,56],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/3","text":""},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"caption","orig":"Table 3: Comparing the efficiency when reduced set and full set of templates are used for template selection","parent":{"$ref":"#/tables/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":185.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":90.0,"r":506.0,"t":222.66666666666663},"charspan":[0,108],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/4","text":"Table 3: Comparing the efficiency when reduced set and full set of templates are used for template selection"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"It can be observed in Table 3 that the efficiency of the proposed method is higher than application domains (with   comparable   results in the   remaining   domains). In   particular, the average efficiency when a reduced set of templates is used is over 25%. gain","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":75.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":87.33333333333333,"r":507.6666666666667,"t":154.33333333333337},"charspan":[0,265],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/5","text":"It can be observed in Table 3 that the efficiency of the proposed method is higher than application domains 